resources.string:
"Choose a WiFi with a strong signal, and fill in the WiFi password correctly to quickly connect the device to the Internet. 
The following problems may cause the device to fail to connect to the Internet, and it is recommended to avoid
1. Check whether the WiFi anti-robbing network is turned on. This setting may cause the device to fail Normal network connection. You can temporarily turn off the anti-robbing network, and then restore the router settings after the device is successfully connected to the Internet; 
2. If your home has a dual-band router, please check whether the WiFi connected to the device is a 5GHz band WiFi, and please allow the device to connect 2.4GHz band WiFi; 
3. The device does not currently support WPA/WPA2 enterprise-level WiFi, please choose other WiFi; 
4. If your home WiFi is bridged, your network may be very unstable due to bridging reasons. Stable, it is recommended to connect to non-bridged WiFi"
